  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\u222c}_{D}x\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{16{x}^{3}}{9}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16(3)^{3}}{9}-0 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
